    <string name="onboarding_title">Welcome to BoxEQ</string>
    <string name="onboarding_intro">BoxEQ equalizes the sound of other apps, such as Telegram and Instagram, by attaching an audio effect to their playback. Please read what it can and cannot do.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_limits_title">Honest limitations</string>
    <string name="onboarding_limit_session">Android only lets BoxEQ equalize an app if BoxEQ knows that app\'s audio session. Apps that announce their session work right away. Many apps, possibly including Telegram and Instagram, do not announce it.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_limit_shizuku">Shizuku mode can find those sessions, but it needs the Shizuku app running (it must be started again after every reboot unless your phone is rooted) and Android 12 or newer.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_limit_device">Some phones do not support the advanced DynamicsProcessing effect. BoxEQ then falls back to the basic equalizer built into the device, with fewer bands and no limiter.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_limit_service">Effects only last while BoxEQ is running. A notification stays visible while it does; please do not disable it.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_limit_scope">Apps that use hardware offload, protected (DRM) audio or their own audio engine may ignore the effect. In that case the status shows that the app does not expose its audio session.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_privacy">BoxEQ has no internet access and never records or stores your audio.</string>
